id: k8s.service.nodeport
kind: kubernetes
title: NodePort service
aliases: nodeport
tags: networking, service
questions:
  - how do you expose a service outside the cluster cheaply?
invariant: The service is reachable on a static port on every node IP, in addition to its ClusterIP.
answer_30s: NodePort opens the same port on every node and forwards to the Service, so any node IP serves as an entry point.
answer_2m: |
  NodePort is NodeIP:port -> Service -> endpoints. It requires you to know node
  IPs and to keep the port in a narrow range (30000-32767 by default), and it
  exposes the port on all nodes whether or not they run the workload. In
  practice it appears under a LoadBalancer or replaced by an Ingress; it stays
  useful as a debugging path when TCP-level access is needed.
when_to_use:
  - quick external access in a lab cluster; debugging TCP reachability
avoid_when:
  - production HTTP traffic (Ingress/LoadBalancer gives names, TLS and fewer open ports)
related:
  - k8s.service.loadbalancer
  - k8s.ingress
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/#type-nodeport
